{"book":58,"chapter":7,"context":{"chapter":7,"title":"Melchizedek, a Priest Forever","summary":"Using the mysterious figure of Melchizedek, the writer shows that Jesus' priesthood is greater than the Levitical priesthood and that he lives forever to intercede for his people.","background":"Melchizedek appears briefly in Genesis 14:18-20 as king of Salem and priest of God Most High, who blessed Abraham and received a tenth of the spoils. Genesis records no family line, birth or death for him, and the writer draws meaning from that silence (v. 3). Since Levi descended from Abraham, the writer argues that Levi in a sense paid tithes to Melchizedek (vv. 9–10).","customs":[{"term":"Names and titles","verses":"7:2","note":"Melchizedek means 'king of righteousness', and Salem means 'peace'."},{"term":"Tithes","verses":"7:4-10","note":"A tenth of produce or spoils given to God's priest. Under the Law, Levites received tithes from Israel (Numbers 18:21)."}],"watchFor":["'He ever liveth to make intercession for them' (v. 25).","Jesus offered himself 'once' (v. 27)."],"connections":["Genesis 14:18-20","Psalms 110:4","Numbers 18:21","Genesis 49:10"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Οὗτος","Houtos","G3778","D-NSM","This"],["γὰρ","gar","G1063","CONJ","for"],["ὁ","ho","G3588","T-NSM","<the>"],["Μελχισέδεκ","Melchisedek","G3198","N-NSM-P","Melchizedek"],["βασιλεὺς","basileus","G935","N-NSM","king"],["Σαλήμ","Salēm","G4532","N-GSF-L","of Salem"],["ἱερεὺς","hi'ereus","G2409","N-NSM","priest"],["τοῦ","tou","G3588","T-GSM","<the>"],["θεοῦ","theou","G2316","N-GSM-T","of God"],["τοῦ","tou","G3588","T-GSM","<the>"],["ὑψίστου","hupsistou","G5310","A-GSM-S","Most High"],["ὁ","ho","G3588","T-NSM","who"],["συναντήσας","sunantēsas","G4876","V-AAP-NSM","having met"],["Ἀβραὰμ","Abraam","G11","N-DSM-P","with Abraham"],["ὑποστρέφοντι","hupostrephonti","G5290","V-PAP-DSM","returning"],["ἀπὸ","apo","G575","PREP","from"],["τῆς","tēs","G3588","T-GSF","the"],["κοπῆς","kopēs","G2871","N-GSF","slaughter"],["τῶν",